      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NOISY GEM (1) was prominent throughout when winning two back but could manage only midfield last time when 4th and beaten 4 lengths at this track (23.36). Rates on top in this line up. JUNO USKO (4) led early but gathered in and found a bit of trouble before filling the minors (23.21) at this track over 395m in a Grade 6. Solid beginner and with a good start can clear the tricky draw. Must include in calculations. TONY (8) produced a modest effort most recently when sixth at The Meadows over 525m behind Kiwi George (31.16) in a Grade 5. Form from his last run is proving strong. Has ability and can atone. SOKAI (2) is sure to play a big role again after a run of minor placings.",
